// bisect: fusion/JIT bug (interp != jit) — FIXED, kept as regress pin.
// After the fix this program is a CompileErr in both modes (AGREE).
// Found by soak aug31e (ryouko fuzz divergence_000000, 2026-08-31).
//
// Pre-fix: interp [f64:-1.] (dynamic `[] - 1`), jit nothing, with the
// kernel logging
//   kernel param `v`: runtime Array([]) doesn't match the compiled
//   Scalar(I64) slot (typechecker static/dynamic mismatch)
//
// Two holes, one witness. (1) `let inner = type M = ..` put a TYPEDEF
// in value position: the node is ⊥-typed with a phantom value channel,
// so `inner` bound at ⊥ — the same class 82e4fbfa closed for `use`/
// static `mod` (aug27a aieka). `type`/`trait`/`impl` are now statement-
// position-only like the rest of the declaration family. (2) The catch
// connect `inner <- array::filter(..)` then ran `⊥ ⊇ <site cell>` in
// contains, whose (Bottom, TVar) arm answered TRUE for a cell ALREADY
// BOUND to Array<string> — and under InitTVars CLOBBERED the binding
// to ⊥. Downstream `v - outer` then typechecked v at i64 while the
// interp routed the filter's arrays through the untyped value channel;
// the kernel froze Scalar(I64) and bottomed every arrival at the ABI.
// The arm now derefs a bound cell (⊥ ⊇ Array refuses, matching the
// literal-RHS refusal); an open cell still commits 'r := ⊥, the one
// solution.
{let outer = never(); catch(e) outer <- i64:1; let g = || {let inner = type M = [`M(Map<string, i64>), `N]; catch(e) inner <- array::filter(["a", "b"], |s| str::len(s) > i64:5); error(`A)?; inner}; let v = g(); error(`B)?; v - outer}
